// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// Draft – not published (MERGED: volatility-spike exclusion) – 4H-DATA / 1H-ALERT variant (v4h-1)
// Grid-Fit Screener (companion to "Crypto Grid Strategy v2"). Educational use only.
// The grid-fit score is a descriptive 0-100 number built from HISTORICAL data (regime, volatility, range containment,
// midline crossings, liquidity). It is not a probability or a forecast of any outcome.
// v4h-1: ALL scoring/signal data comes from the 4h timeframe (input "Source timeframe", default "240") while the
// script runs and alerts on the 1h chart (one alert per 1h bar close).
// Repaint control: request.security(sym, "240", f_metrics(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on) where f_metrics()
// returns only [1]-offset values. With lookahead_on + [1], every 1h bar sees the LAST COMPLETED 4h bar, on history
// and in realtime alike (TradingView's documented non-repainting HTF pattern). Values change only when a new 4h
// bar has completed (i.e. on the first 1h bar after a 4h close).
//@version=6
indicator("Grid-Fit Screener – Draft", shorttitle = "GridFit", overlay = false)

string G_S = "Symbols (36 + 1 chart = 37 request.security calls – limit is 40 per script)"
string G_P = "Scoring"
string G_A = "Alert"

